---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../utils/url';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import hero from '../../assets/articles/plate-solving.jpg';
---

<Layout
  title="Plate Solving and Metadata"
  description="What is plate solving and what metadata it generates for astrophotography images."
  descriptionIt="Cos'è il plate solving e quali metadati genera per le immagini di astrofotografia."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <h1 data-lang-en class="ps-heading ps-heading--hero mt-6 text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">What is Plate Solving?</h1>
    <h1 data-lang-it class="ps-heading ps-heading--hero mt-6 text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">Cos'è il Plate Solving?</h1>

    <div class="ps-image-wrap mt-8 w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10">
      <Image quality={90} src={hero} alt="Plate solving" class="ps-image w-full" />
    </div>

    <div class="prose-astro mt-10">
      <div data-lang-en class="ps-typewriter">
        <p>
          <strong>Plate solving</strong> is the process that determines the celestial coordinates of an
          astronomical image by matching the detected star positions with those of a reference catalog. The
          operation computes the transformation between pixel coordinates and spherical coordinates, assigning
          Right Ascension (RA) and Declination (DEC) values to every point.
        </p>
        <p>This procedure is essential for several applications:</p>
        <p>
          - <strong>Object identification</strong>: Automatic recognition of point-like and extended sources
          (stars, galaxies, nebulae).<br />
          - <strong>Alignment and stacking</strong>: Overlaying sequential frames to increase the
          signal-to-noise ratio.<br />
          - <strong>Astrometric calibration</strong>: Definition of the World Coordinate System (WCS)
          required for rigorous positional measurements.<br />
          - <strong>Pointing correction</strong>: Detection and correction of positioning errors in automatic
          Go-To pointing systems.<br />
          - <strong>Variability and transient detection</strong>: Photometric monitoring and tracking of
          asteroids, comets, or events such as supernovae.
        </p>

        <p><strong>Generated metadata</strong><br />
          Running plate solving enriches the image file with structured parameters, grouped into the
          following categories:
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Astrometric parameters</strong> (derived from the computation):<br />
          - Field center coordinates (RA, DEC).<br />
          - Field of view (FOV), expressed in arcminutes or degrees.<br />
          - Image scale (resolution in arcseconds per pixel).<br />
          - Rotation angle of the axis relative to celestial north.<br />
          - WCS transformation matrix.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Observation parameters</strong> (file header):<br />
          - Acquisition date and time (UTC or Julian Date).<br />
          - Integration time (exposure).<br />
          - Optics and sensor specifications (aperture, focal length, pixel size).<br />
          - Selective or narrowband filters used (e.g. Hα, LRGB).
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Photometric and reference parameters</strong>:<br />
          - Zero-point calibration for magnitude.<br />
          - Reference star catalog (e.g. Gaia, UCAC4, Tycho-2).
        </p>

        <p><strong>Formats and tools</strong><br />
          Metadata is mainly written into the headers of files in FITS format (Flexible Image Transport
          System), the standard for professional astronomy, or saved as overlaid vectors on rasterized images
          (JPEG/PNG) by remote solving services.
        </p>
        <p><span class="ps-highlight">Metadata inspection and analysis:</span><br />
          - <a href="https://sites.google.com/cfa.harvard.edu/saoimageds9" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>SAOImage DS9</strong></a><br />
          - <a href="https://aladin.cds.unistra.fr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Aladin Sky Atlas</strong></a><br />
          - <a href="https://www.astropy.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>astropy</strong></a>
        </p>
        <p><span class="ps-highlight">Online plate solving:</span><br />
          - <a href="http://nova.astrometry.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Astrometry.net</strong></a>
        </p>
        <p><span class="ps-highlight">Local plate solving:</span><br />
          - <a href="https://www.hnsky.org/astap.htm/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>ASTAP</strong></a> (Astrometric Stacking Program)<br />
          - <a href="https://pixinsight.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>PixInsight</strong></a> (ImageSolver script)
        </p>
      </div>

      <div data-lang-it class="ps-typewriter">
        <p>
          Il <strong>plate solving</strong> è il procedimento che determina le coordinate celesti di
          un'immagine astronomica confrontando le posizioni stellari rilevate con quelle di un catalogo di
          riferimento. L'operazione calcola la trasformazione tra le coordinate dei pixel e quelle sferiche,
          assegnando a ogni punto i valori di Ascensione Retta (RA) e Declinazione (DEC).
        </p>
        <p>La procedura è fondamentale per diverse applicazioni:</p>
        <p>
          - <strong>Identificazione di oggetti</strong>: Riconoscimento automatico di sorgenti puntiformi ed
          estese (stelle, galassie, nebulose).<br />
          - <strong>Allineamento e stacking</strong>: Sovrapposizione di fotogrammi sequenziali per
          incrementare il rapporto segnale/rumore.<br />
          - <strong>Calibrazione astrometrica</strong>: Definizione del Sistema di Coordinate Mondiali (WCS)
          necessario per misurazioni posizionali rigorose.<br />
          - <strong>Correzione di puntamento</strong>: Riscontro e correzione degli errori di posizionamento
          nei sistemi di puntamento automatico (Go-To).<br />
          - <strong>Rilevamento di variabilità e transienti</strong>: Monitoraggio fotometrico e tracciamento
          di asteroidi, comete o eventi quali supernove.
        </p>

        <p><strong>Metadati generati</strong><br />
          L'esecuzione del plate solving integra il file dell'immagine con parametri strutturati, suddivisi
          nelle seguenti categorie:
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Parametri astrometrici</strong> (derivati dal calcolo):<br />
          - Coordinate del centro campo (RA, DEC).<br />
          - Campo inquadrato (FOV), espresso in minuti o gradi d'arco.<br />
          - Scala dell'immagine (risoluzione in secondi d'arco per pixel).<br />
          - Angolo di rotazione dell'asse rispetto al nord celeste.<br />
          - Matrice di trasformazione WCS.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Parametri di osservazione</strong> (intestazione del file):<br />
          - Data e ora di acquisizione (UTC o Data Giuliana).<br />
          - Tempo di integrazione (esposizione).<br />
          - Specifiche ottiche e del sensore (apertura, lunghezza focale, dimensione pixel).<br />
          - Filtri selettivi o a banda stretta impiegati (es. Hα, LRGB).
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Parametri fotometrici e di riferimento</strong>:<br />
          - Calibrazione zero-point per la magnitudine.<br />
          - Catalogo stellare di confronto (es. Gaia, UCAC4, Tycho-2).
        </p>

        <p><strong>Formati e strumenti</strong><br />
          I metadati vengono scritti principalmente negli header dei file in formato FITS (Flexible Image
          Transport System), lo standard per l'astronomia professionale, o salvati come vettori sovrapposti
          su immagini rastrizzate (JPEG/PNG) da servizi di risoluzione remota.
        </p>
        <p><span class="ps-highlight">Ispezione e analisi dei metadati:</span><br />
          - <a href="https://sites.google.com/cfa.harvard.edu/saoimageds9" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>SAOImage DS9</strong></a><br />
          - <a href="https://aladin.cds.unistra.fr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Aladin Sky Atlas</strong></a><br />
          - <a href="https://www.astropy.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>astropy</strong></a>
        </p>
        <p><span class="ps-highlight">Plate solving online:</span><br />
          - <a href="http://nova.astrometry.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Astrometry.net</strong></a>
        </p>
        <p><span class="ps-highlight">Plate solving locale:</span><br />
          - <a href="https://www.hnsky.org/astap.htm/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>ASTAP</strong></a> (Astrometric Stacking Program)<br />
          - <a href="https://pixinsight.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>PixInsight</strong></a> (script ImageSolver)
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 flex justify-center">
      <a href={withBase('/video-utility/')} class="btn-accent justify-center min-w-[190px]">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path d="M19 12H5M11 6l-6 6 6 6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
        </svg>
        <span data-lang-en>Back to Video &amp; Utility</span>
        <span data-lang-it>Torna a Video &amp; Utility</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .ps-highlight {
    color: #facc15;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .ps-heading {
    perspective: 600px;
  }

  .ps-heading .ps-char-mask {
    display: inline-block;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .ps-heading .ps-char {
    display: inline-block;
    will-change: transform, filter, opacity;
  }

  /* Avoid a flash of unanimated text: hidden until JS wraps + reveals it. */
  .ps-heading {
    visibility: hidden;
  }

  .ps-heading.ps-ready {
    visibility: visible;
  }

  .ps-image-wrap {
    overflow: hidden;
    perspective: 900px;
  }

  .ps-image {
    display: block;
    will-change: transform, filter, opacity;
    visibility: hidden;
  }

  .ps-image.ps-ready {
    visibility: visible;
  }

  /* Avoid a flash of the full untyped text before the typewriter script runs. */
  .ps-typewriter {
    visibility: hidden;
  }

  .ps-typewriter.ps-ready {
    visibility: visible;
  }

  .ps-tw-cursor {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 2px;
    height: 1em;
    vertical-align: -0.15em;
    background: var(--color-accent, #7dd3fc);
    margin-left: 2px;
    animation: ps-tw-blink 0.8s step-end infinite;
  }

  @keyframes ps-tw-blink {
    0%,
    100% {
      opacity: 1;
    }
    50% {
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }
</style>

<noscript>
  <style>
    .ps-heading,
    .ps-image,
    .ps-typewriter {
      visibility: visible;
    }
  </style>
</noscript>

<script>
  import { gsap } from 'gsap';

  const LETTER_STAGGER = 0.09;

  function wrapChars(el: HTMLElement) {
    const text = el.textContent ?? '';
    el.textContent = '';
    const chars: HTMLElement[] = [];
    [...text].forEach((ch) => {
      const mask = document.createElement('span');
      mask.className = 'ps-char-mask';
      const charEl = document.createElement('span');
      charEl.className = 'ps-char';
      charEl.textContent = ch === ' ' ? ' ' : ch;
      mask.appendChild(charEl);
      el.appendChild(mask);
      chars.push(charEl);
    });
    return chars;
  }

  function animateIn(chars: HTMLElement[]) {
    gsap.fromTo(
      chars,
      {
        opacity: 0,
        scale: 1.7,
        skewX: -18,
        rotateY: 25,
        filter: 'blur(10px)',
      },
      {
        opacity: 1,
        scale: 1,
        skewX: 0,
        rotateY: 0,
        filter: 'blur(0px)',
        duration: 1.8,
        ease: 'elastic.out(1, 0.4)',
        stagger: LETTER_STAGGER,
      }
    );
  }

  function animateImageIn(img: HTMLElement, onSettled?: () => void) {
    img.classList.add('ps-ready');
    // Blur/opacity settle once, smoothly (a bouncing blur reads as a glitch);
    // the scale gets a single soft overshoot, no skew/rotate — those 3D
    // transforms are what made the image look blurry while it moved.
    gsap.fromTo(
      img,
      { opacity: 0, filter: 'blur(14px)' },
      { opacity: 1, filter: 'blur(0px)', duration: 1.4, ease: 'power2.out', delay: 0.4 }
    );
    gsap.fromTo(
      img,
      { scale: 1.06 },
      {
        scale: 1,
        duration: 2.2,
        ease: 'back.out(1.2)',
        delay: 0.4,
        onComplete: onSettled,
      }
    );
  }

  function whenImageLoaded(img: HTMLImageElement, cb: () => void) {
    if (img.complete && img.naturalWidth > 0) {
      cb();
    } else {
      img.addEventListener('load', () => cb(), { once: true });
    }
  }

  function setup() {
    // Guarded with data attributes so this is safe to call again on every
    // astro:page-load (needed because view-transition back/forward
    // navigation can restore this page without re-running its script).
    const heroes = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.ps-heading--hero:not([data-tw-inited])');
    heroes.forEach((el) => {
      el.dataset.twInited = 'true';
      const chars = wrapChars(el);
      el.classList.add('ps-ready');
      animateIn(chars);
    });

    watchLangSwitch();

    const freshImage = document.querySelector<HTMLImageElement>('.ps-image:not([data-img-inited])');
    if (freshImage) {
      freshImage.dataset.imgInited = 'true';
      // Wait for the photo to actually load, then let it settle into place,
      // and only then start typing the description.
      whenImageLoaded(freshImage, () => {
        animateImageIn(freshImage, () => setTimeout(typeActiveDescription, 900));
      });
    } else {
      // No image to wait for (already animated on a prior run, or absent).
      typeActiveDescription();
    }
  }

  // ---- Typewriter effect for the description text (keeps bold/links/line breaks) ----
  // Tune these once we settle on timing/duration.
  const TYPEWRITER_BASE_MS = 2.5;
  const TYPEWRITER_VARIANCE_MS = 1.5;

  type TwToken =
    | { kind: 'open'; tag: string; attrs: string }
    | { kind: 'close'; tag: string }
    | { kind: 'char'; value: string };

  function escapeHtmlChar(ch: string) {
    if (ch === '&') return '&amp;';
    if (ch === '<') return '&lt;';
    if (ch === '>') return '&gt;';
    return ch;
  }

  function tokenizeHtml(root: HTMLElement): TwToken[] {
    const tokens: TwToken[] = [];
    function walk(node: ChildNode) {
      if (node.nodeType === Node.TEXT_NODE) {
        for (const ch of node.textContent ?? '') tokens.push({ kind: 'char', value: ch });
        return;
      }
      if (node.nodeType !== Node.ELEMENT_NODE) return;
      const el = node as HTMLElement;
      const attrs = [...el.attributes]
        .map((a) => `${a.name}="${a.value.replace(/"/g, '&quot;')}"`)
        .join(' ');
      tokens.push({ kind: 'open', tag: el.tagName.toLowerCase(), attrs });
      el.childNodes.forEach(walk);
      tokens.push({ kind: 'close', tag: el.tagName.toLowerCase() });
    }
    root.childNodes.forEach(walk);
    return tokens;
  }

  // Renders tokens up to `charCount` visible characters, auto-closing any
  // tag still open at that point so the partial markup stays valid.
  function renderTokens(tokens: TwToken[], charCount: number): string {
    let html = '';
    let shown = 0;
    const stack: string[] = [];
    for (const tok of tokens) {
      if (tok.kind === 'char') {
        if (shown >= charCount) break;
        html += escapeHtmlChar(tok.value);
        shown++;
      } else if (tok.kind === 'open') {
        html += `<${tok.tag}${tok.attrs ? ' ' + tok.attrs : ''}>`;
        stack.push(tok.tag);
      } else {
        html += `</${tok.tag}>`;
        stack.pop();
      }
    }
    while (stack.length) html += `</${stack.pop()}>`;
    return html;
  }

  function runTypewriter(container: HTMLElement) {
    const tokens = tokenizeHtml(container);
    const totalChars = tokens.filter((t) => t.kind === 'char').length;
    const cursor = '<span class="ps-tw-cursor">&nbsp;</span>';

    container.innerHTML = '';
    container.classList.add('ps-ready');

    let i = 0;
    function type() {
      if (i <= totalChars) {
        container.innerHTML = renderTokens(tokens, i) + cursor;
        i++;
        const delay =
          TYPEWRITER_BASE_MS + (Math.random() * TYPEWRITER_VARIANCE_MS * 2 - TYPEWRITER_VARIANCE_MS);
        setTimeout(type, delay);
      } else {
        container.querySelector('.ps-tw-cursor')?.remove();
        container.dataset.typed = 'done';
      }
    }
    type();
  }

  function typeIfNeeded(el: HTMLElement | null) {
    if (!el || el.dataset.typed === 'done' || el.dataset.typed === 'running') return;
    el.dataset.typed = 'running';
    runTypewriter(el);
  }

  function currentLang(): 'it' | 'en' {
    return document.documentElement.getAttribute('data-lang') === 'en' ? 'en' : 'it';
  }

  function typeActiveDescription() {
    const lang = currentLang();
    const el = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`.ps-typewriter[data-lang-${lang}]`);
    typeIfNeeded(el);
  }

  function watchLangSwitch() {
    const win = window as unknown as { __psLangObserver?: MutationObserver };
    win.__psLangObserver?.disconnect();
    win.__psLangObserver = new MutationObserver(() => typeActiveDescription());
    win.__psLangObserver.observe(document.documentElement, {
      attributes: true,
      attributeFilter: ['data-lang'],
    });
  }

  setup();
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', setup);
</script>
